same place on 28th. In October a fair number of records; fifty 
on 21st at Rhinns of Islay, and a number on 11th at Lochindaul ; 
twenty at Mull of Galloway on 20th. 

Woodcock—At Lamlash, on 15th March, two birds at 11 A.M. ; 
E., strong; and on February 1st, one at Kyleakin, 11.30 a..; 
S., with snow on the island. 

No more entries till October, when only three in all at Rona 
(on 8th), S.E., fresh, “first seen;” one at Rhinns of Islay (22d), 
N.E.; and one at Corsewall (25th), N.E., fresh, “struck and 
killed.” In November, one bird at Mull of Galloway on 19th; 
and one, on 20th and 21st December, at Rhinns of Islay.
